{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling for S4 and every later head: a focused run is a working run.\nRun it with the plain commands of docs/testing.md.\n\nS4 opened its first compiler unit at 07:12. At 11:24 the Native\ntests have not passed, and no gate has started. Eight booked units\nfailed in that time. Six failed on a stale fixture or inventory.\nOne never launched. The last, 8598df1a, failed in its own metadata\nbinder before any test ran. One failure found a real defect: the\ndropped model-only visibility in views/tools.ts.\n\ndocs/testing.md, \"Run the tests of what you changed\", gives the\ncommands: npm run test:changed, or npx vitest run --project \u003cname\u003e\n\u003cfile\u003e. Its evidence rule names two things: the gate at the head you\nsend, and one or two honest controls for each invariant.\n\nSo from now on:\n\n1. A focused run before the gate claims nothing. Run the failing\n   owners with the plain command. Read the exit and the failures.\n   Repair. Run again. A repeat of a passing owner is allowed.\n2. A focused run needs no metadata binder, no source receipt, no\n   independent peer review of its launcher, and no sealed output\n   directory. Its output may go to a scratch directory.\n3. The validation slot rule stays. File one START line and one END\n   line for each run, two or three sentences each, so that no two\n   bodies run at once on this machine.\n4. The evidence care stays where the evidence is: the one gate at\n   the review head, the controls with their planned reds, the\n   Transport check, and the Card push run.\n5. Do not carry a focused pass from one head to another. The gate at\n   the final head covers every owner, so nothing needs a carry.\n\nFor S4 now: run the 58 Native tests and the 48 Plain tests at\n6c379107 with the plain command, and repair until they pass. Then\nbook the gate.\n\nTell me in one act if a rule from Hugh or the checker requires the\nbinder for a working run. I know of none.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}